      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$ contains the positive integers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{C}$ contains all complex numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{C}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{R}$, $\\mathbb{C}$ only.",
