    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1b9a838d-317b-5e3b-b9ee-e15c3107c671",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the negative integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$ contains the positive real numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{C}$ contains all complex numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{C}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative integers.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{R}$, $\\mathbb{C}$ only.",
