      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the positive integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the positive integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}^{-}$ contains the negative real numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the positive integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the positive integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive integers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the positive integers.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{R}$ only.",
