      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the nonnegative integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the nonnegative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}_0$ contains the nonnegative integers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{N}_0$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}$ contains all rational numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{N}_0$, $\\mathbb{Q}$, $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$, $\\mathbb{Z}$ only.",
